# =========================================================================
# fleet/mod — distributed fleet coordination, GPU scheduling, and multi-node
# orchestration.
#
# Parity oracle: rust-old/src/fleet/mod.rs
#
# Node registry with heartbeat-based liveness, 5 placement policies, GPU VRAM
# tracking and allocation, distributed crew state with barrier sync, and fleet
# coordination with failover.
#
# This module is the hub mirroring mod.rs: it carries no logic of its own, only
# the include order. Resolution is single-pass and callees must precede callers,
# so the order below is a DEPENDENCY order, not the oracle's declaration order —
# `cost_planning`, `environment` and `discovery` are leaves; `registry` defines
# the node vocabulary `placement`, `gpu`, `state` and `coordinator` all speak.
#
# Every price, rate, score and cost in this group is an f64 carried as its
# IEEE-754 bit pattern in an i64 — compare with f64_lt / f64_gt / f64_eq,
# never with the integer operators.
#
# ⚠ INCOMPLETE — this hub grows one line per bite. The oracle declares eleven
# submodules; the lines below are the ones that exist. Still to land:
# environment, discovery, topology, registry, placement, gpu, state, relay,
# federation, coordinator. Do not read a missing line as a decision.
# =========================================================================

